  "created": "2026-11-09T11:04:10.02Z",
  "description": "Secure, zero-dependency dynamic sorting for IQueryable (EF Core, LINQ providers) and IEnumerable by property name or sort expression (\"name desc, price\"), with allow-list protection, nested properties and automatic ThenBy chaining.",
  "id": "Fayakun.Extensions.DynamicSorting",
  "isPrerelease": false,
  "lastEdited": "2026-11-09T11:08:01.64Z",
  "licenseExpression": "MIT",
  "licenseUrl": "https://licenses.nuget.org/MIT",
  "listed": true,
  "packageHash": "GvWZIuaHaMANjXr3sNdTSLQVzN9pbCyaSL3TOd+MWWNMBNrMnmV/I1DJWQIRap7/Mv9/eWAo2Y7MhveLEBNcHg==",
  "packageHashAlgorithm": "SHA512",
  "packageSize": 93940,
  "published": "2026-11-09T11:04:10.02Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v1.1.0\n- New targets: netstandard1.1, netstandard2.1 and netcoreapp3.1.\n- New: sort expressions such as \"name desc, -price, createdAt asc\" via ApplySorting(sortExpression, allowedFields).\n- New: nested property paths such as \"Customer.Name\" (null-safe for in-memory collections).\n- New: IEnumerable<string> allow-list overloads (for example a HashSet shared across requests).\n- Fix: the first sort on AsQueryable() sources (EnumerableQuery) and similar providers was emitted as ThenBy instead of OrderBy and failed when run. \"Already ordered\" is now detected from the expression tree.\n- Fix: property names are now matched case-insensitively, consistent with the allow-list. Previously \"price\" passed the allow-list and then threw.\n- Faster: in-memory key selectors are compiled once per type and property, then cached.",
